# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown
# `CONNECTOR-IDENTITY-KEY`: the VERSION GATE on `id=`, ACCEPTING half. The five
# directive lines below are BYTE-IDENTICAL to case 812's first section; the
# header is the only thing that differs, `0.4` → `0.5`, and this document
# parses CLEAN.
#
# What the model pins, beyond the fact that it parses: `id` is projected FIRST
# on the edges that carry it and is ABSENT — not null, not empty — on the one
# that does not. Anonymity is the language's default and the missing key is its
# whole statement, so an engine that emitted `"id": null` for the anonymous
# connector would fail here, and so would one that accepted the key and
# discarded the value.
figdown 0.5 block
node a "A"
node b "B"
node c "C"
edge a -> b id=e1
edge b -> c id=e2
# The third connector is ANONYMOUS, on purpose: `id=` is OPTIONAL, and a
# document that names two of its three connectors is the ordinary case, not a
# half-migrated one.
edge a -> c
